AIHawk includes or adapts work from these projects.

src/aihawk/documents.py
  The shape of the job report (dimensions weighed by judgment, a score from 1 to 5, posting legitimacy
  judged apart from the score) is adapted from career-ops (https://github.com/santifer/career-ops),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Santiago Fernandez de Valderrama. No file was copied.

src/aihawk/profile.py, src/aihawk/database.py
  The search plan's rules and the rarity weight follow the planner of the LLDB engine by the same author.

The published job database
  Is merged from the public sources named in pipeline/build.py, each with its home and licence as far as
  it states one; each release's manifest.json lists them, with the rows each gave or the error that left
  it out that day, and every row names the sources that carried it. Each posting belongs to its employer and links back to the original.
